- * Bit 0 of that register is UTMI_PHY_SUSPEND_N, and it was clear, i.e. the
- * wrapper was holding the high-speed PHY's UTMI interface in suspend. That
- * sits upstream of every hypothesis tried so far. A suspended UTMI block
- * hands the controller no UTMI clock; a controller with no UTMI clock still
- * retires DEPSTARTCFG, which is driven by the bus clock, but never finishes
